{"step_index":2984,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:21:29Z","input_tokens":232166,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1118,"content":"Here are tailored descriptions you can directly copy-paste into your **Resume**, **Portfolio Website**, and **LinkedIn**:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Resume Section (Project / Experience Entry)\n\n**Teach Me This Code — Visual Python Execution & DSA Learning Platform**  \n*Technologies: JavaScript (ES6+), Python AST Execution Engine, HTML5/CSS3, IndexedDB, LocalStorage*\n\n- Engineered an offline-first educational platform and step-by-step Python execution visualizer modeling runtime stack frames, heap references, and granular expression evaluation.\n- Architected a 300-problem curated DSA catalog covering 30 topics and a 10-stage learning roadmap, complete with rule-based pattern guides and 900+ client-side test cases.\n- Developed an in-browser code editor with instant test validation, dual-approach reference solutions (baseline vs. optimal), and an interactive bridge to the execution visualizer.\n- Built a zero-cloud local persistence engine leveraging `localStorage` and `IndexedDB` with automated schema validation, corruption guards, and JSON backup export/merge.\n- Authored a comprehensive test suite of 3,300+ automated unit and integration tests, ensuring 100% pass rates and strict regression-free engine execution.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Portfolio Website Summary (Project Card / Detail Page)\n\n> **Headline:** An offline-first, beginner-friendly DSA learning academy and interactive Python code execution visualizer.\n>\n> **Project Overview:**  \n> Most beginner developers struggle to connect abstract Data Structures & Algorithms concepts with what physically happens in computer memory during execution. **Teach Me This Code** solves this by providing a dedicated problem learning workspace combined with a Thonny-style line-by-line visual stepper that tracks heap allocations, variable mutations, and loop conditions in real time.\n>\n> **Key Engineering Highlights:**\n> - **Self-Contained & Private:** Built with zero external AI APIs, paid dependencies, or cloud backends; runs 100% client-side in the browser.\n> - **Curated 300-Problem Catalog:** Structured progression across 30 core DSA topics and 10 difficulty stages with instant test runners and plain-English complexity breakdowns.\n> - **Resilient Local Storage:** Implemented offline state synchronization using LocalStorage and IndexedDB snapshots, with full export/import backup validation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Quick Elevator Pitch / LinkedIn Post Summary\n\n> Built **Teach Me This Code**, a client-side Data Structures & Algorithms learning platform and Python execution visualizer. It helps learners master 300 curated DSA problems by stepping through execution line-by-line to see variables, heap memory, and condition checks in real time—all with zero external cloud dependencies, 100% local computer storage, and 3,300+ automated regression tests.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Recommended Tech Stack Tags\n\n`JavaScript (Vanilla ES6+)` • `Python` • `Interactive Data Visualization` • `Client-Side Execution Engine` • `IndexedDB / LocalStorage` • `Responsive UI/UX` • `Automated Unit Testing`","thinking":"Here's the breakdown for the user's project inclusion:\n\n1.  **Resume Bullets**:\n    *   Developed a learning platform and visualizer, resulting in a 25% increase in user engagement with DSA concepts.\n    *   Implemented interactive code execution and visualization tools, boosting comprehension scores by 15%.\n    *   Designed and maintained the project, incorporating feedback and expanding features, to meet the evolving needs of learners.\n    *   Utilized [Relevant Tech Stack] to build a robust and user-friendly platform that is easily scalable.\n\n2.  **Portfolio Project Summary**:\n    This project arose to tackle the frequent stumbling blocks in learning data structures and algorithms, which often result from a lack of immediate, visual feedback. I aimed to bridge this gap with an interactive platform. The goal was to build a tool not just for theoretical understanding but also for practical coding proficiency, making DSA approachable. The success metrics were increased engagement and comprehension, which was measured through user interaction.\n\n\n"}
