entering stepper controls or distributing elements between the primary and secondary bars, should be evaluated to improve the layout. Analysis indicates that the `brand-area` div contains the step information and the \"GLOBAL SCOPE\" label, which appears disconnected from the intended arrow visualization in the current design.\n\n\nThe `space-between` alignment in the top bar creates excessive horizontal space due to only two elements being present. This pushes content to the edges, resulting in a large gap on wider screens. The arrows potentially highlight the areas adjacent to the code display, which would include the large empty regions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css\"","EndLine":"340","StartLine":"310","toolAction":"\"Viewing overview strip CSS\"","toolSummary":"\"View overview-strip CSS\""}}]}
