{"step_index":3004,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-28T16:53:52Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. 6. Phase 4: Add Problem Search and Filters\n\nImplement functional search and filtering.\n\nUsers must be able to filter by:\n\nTopic.\n\nDifficulty: Easy, Medium, Hard.\n\nStatus: Not Started, Attempted, Solved, Review.\n\nAlgorithmic pattern.\n\nBookmarked status.\n\nAdd sorting by title, difficulty, and learning order.\n\nProvide pagination or efficient list rendering so the catalog remains responsive.\n\nEach problem should have a unique route or detail view. Prevent duplicate records when importing additional problems.\n2. 7. Phase 5: Create a Problem Learning Workspace\n\nWhen a user opens a problem, display a dedicated learning page.\n\nA. Understand the Problem\n\nExplain the problem in simple English.\n\nShow:\n\nWhat the problem asks.\n\nInput and output examples.\n\nExpected output for each example.\n\nImportant constraints.\n\nEdge cases.\n\nWhat the learner needs to calculate or return.\n\nDo not immediately reveal the solution.\n\nB. Learn the Pattern\n\nExplain:\n\nWhich DSA pattern is relevant.\n\nWhy the pattern is useful.\n\nWhich prerequisite concepts are needed.\n\nA small illustrative example.\n\nA simple explanation of the intended approach.\n\nUse built-in, rule-based teaching content. Do not call an AI API.\n\nC. Try It Yourself\n\nProvide a Python editor where the user can write their own solution.\n\nInclude:\n\nRun Code.\n\nRun Tests.\n\nReset Code.\n\nShow Hints.\n\nReveal Reference Solution, with confirmation.\n\nView Test Results.\n\nUse a safe, restricted execution environment. Never execute unrestricted user code on the main application server.\n\nIf the existing execution infrastructure cannot safely support arbitrary Python, implement a restricted interpreter for supported syntax or clearly document the limitation.\n\nD. Visualize Execution\n\nInte\n<truncated 14325 bytes>\n685829300_6748f239.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-11T02:33:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1792931192636_b58462da]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1792931192636_b58462da.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-25T12:27:20Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1792933167216_ce44370c]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1792933167216_ce44370c.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-25T13:12:18Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1792933206684_5c9077d7]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1792933206684_5c9077d7.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-25T13:12:18Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1792933233429_ea028ff0]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1792933233429_ea028ff0.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-25T13:12:18Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1792940520679_827160c7]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1792940520679_827160c7.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-25T15:04:21Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1792940561101_79ae3dd9]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1792940561101_79ae3dd9.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-25T15:04:21Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1793205860585_d1f459c2]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1793205860585_d1f459c2.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-28T16:49:54Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/impl